From 40d38696af49d203e52983238cc6f8a71573ed64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:18:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban-sync): hub CPU reports survive process stalls and
 gateway restarts [daveey]

hermes-hub 2026-11-12 (PR #1429 live probe, run 5 and runs 1-3):

- 13:41:46-13:42:11, 13:42:12-13:42:46 and 13:42:58-13:43:26 the whole gateway
  process stalled (control loop blocked 24.4 s; the advisory sampler's own
  windows 25.3/34.2/27.8 s; worker.persist 25.2 s). The sender shares no lock
  with the Board round that hung; it froze with everything else. Its late ticks
  at 13:42:12 and 13:43:27 ran ~0.3 s before the sampler's restarted window
  closed and sent the hub row CPU-less, erasing its triple, and the half-period
  guard then skipped the next anchor (skipped=1/2).
  * report_tick waits at most CPU_WAIT_S (1.5 s) for the sampler's next sample
    (AdvisorySampler.wait_fresh); never on the loop thread.
  * While the root gate is ON a CPU-less report is withheld unless nothing was
    sent for KEEPALIVE_S (30 s, inside the Board's 90 s stale limit); the
    sender logs `metrics_sender withheld ...` and counts withheld=N.
  * A late send less than half a period before the next anchor delays that
    tick until it is spaced instead of skipping it.
  * The loop's takeover while ON (sender stalled or dead) sends through the
    sender's bounded 2 s transport, not the kept-alive Hub's 30 s path.
  * The stall WARNING no longer claims "the sync loop reports meanwhile"; it
    says whether a tick is in flight (PR #1429 review nit).
- Each of the 7 core-update restarts: the root gateway found a profile gateway
  (askeve-reviewer/-builder) holding .sync.lock, posted its root claim, then
  slept the full 30 s retry (contention 30-31 s every time). A root lease with
  its claim posted now retries every ROOT_CLAIM_RETRY_SECONDS (2 s).

Tests: bare skipif -> platforms("linux") marker (review nit). The
`metrics_sender send` line keys are unchanged.
